  "articleBody": "It's easy to make a few missteps when hiring for handyman tasks, but a little foresight can save you a lot of hassle. One common mistake is not getting a clear, written scope of work. A vague conversation can lead to misunderstandings later on about what's actually being done. Another big one is accepting vague pricing. Always ask for a written quote that details the costs, whether it's hourly or by the project. Don't assume a handyman can handle highly regulated work like complex plumbing or electrical without verifying their qualifications and local rules; that's when a licensed specialist might be necessary. Also, failing to check references or look at prior work can leave you with less-than-stellar results. With HH Remodeling LLC, we pride ourselves on transparency and reliability, so we make sure you're informed every step of the way. We focus on providing peace of mind, not just repairs. Don't leave your home repairs to chance—ask the right questions upfront!",
